3. PURPOSE
The primary purpose of the Job Recruitment System is to provide an efficient, accessible,
and fully digital platform for conducting recruitment processes. The specific objectives are:
• To eliminate the need for physical presence during job recruitment.
• To enable candidates to register, apply, and undergo evaluation through a single
mobile application.
• To automate the extraction of skills from uploaded CVs, reducing manual effort.
• To provide personalized and skill-based job recommendations to candidates.
• To assist HR personnel in screening, approving, and evaluating candidates
efficiently.
• To make the recruitment process transparent, fair, and time-saving for all
stakeholders.
• To create a centralized platform that connects job seekers and recruiters
seamlessly.
4. SCOPE OF THE PROJECT
The Job Recruitment System is designed to serve two primary user groups: Job Seekers
and HR Personnel. The scope of this project encompasses the following functionalities:
 Candidate (Job Seeker) Scope
• Secure registration and account creation with unique credentials.
• Email-based login — username and password delivered to the candidate's email
upon registration.
• CV upload in supported formats through the mobile application.
• Automatic skill extraction from the uploaded CV using text processing.
• Display of relevant job vacancies filtered based on extracted skills.
• Direct job application submission through the platform.
• Participation in MCQ-based evaluation test if shortlisted by HR.
 HR Scope
• Secure HR login and dashboard access.
• Review of candidate profiles and uploaded CVs.
• Approval or rejection of candidate applications.
• Conducting MCQ-based evaluation for approved candidates.
• Evaluation of test results and final hiring decision.
