6. OVERALL DESCRIPTION
 Product Perspective
The Job Recruitment System is a standalone mobile application built using the Flutter
framework. It is designed to work efficiently on both Android and iOS platforms and provides
a responsive, intuitive interface accessible to users with minimal technical knowledge.
The system integrates multiple core functionalities — including user authentication, CV
management, skill extraction, job recommendation, and recruitment evaluation — into a
single, unified mobile platform. It communicates with a backend server using REST APIs,
ensuring secure and efficient data exchange.
• Clean and modern user interface with easy navigation.
• Secure authentication using email-based credential delivery.
• Efficient data handling and CV processing.
• Scalable architecture allowing future feature additions.
 Product Functions
The key functions of the Job Recruitment System include:
• User registration and secure email-based login.
• CV upload and server-side storage.
• Automatic extraction of skills from uploaded CV.
• Skill-based job vacancy recommendations.
• Job application submission by candidates.
• HR review and approval/rejection of candidate applications.
• MCQ-based candidate evaluation and scoring.
• Final hiring decision by HR based on test performance.
7. USER CLASSES AND CHARACTERISTICS
 Job Seeker (Candidate)
The job seeker is the primary end-user of the application. They interact with the system to
find and apply for jobs that match their skills. Upon registration, they receive login credentials
via email. They can upload their CV, view personalized job recommendations, and submit
applications. If selected by HR, they attend an MCQ test within the app. Job seekers are
expected to have basic smartphone usage knowledge.
 HR Personnel
The HR personnel act as the administrator of the recruitment process. They have the
authority to log in to a dedicated HR dashboard, review submitted CVs, and make approval
or rejection decisions. HR users can conduct MCQ evaluations and finalize hiring decisions
based on candidate performance. They are expected to be familiar with digital tools and the
standard recruitment workflow.
8. GENERAL CONSTRAINTS
• A stable internet connection is required for the application to function properly.
• The application must run smoothly on Android and iOS mobile devices.
• Uploaded CVs must be in supported and readable formats for skill extraction.
• All user data must be securely stored and protected from unauthorized access.
• The system must support multiple concurrent users without performance
degradation.
9. ASSUMPTIONS AND DEPENDENCIES
• Users must possess a valid and active email address for registration.
• Candidates must have access to a smartphone with Android or iOS operating
system.
• The system is dependent on consistent internet connectivity for all operations.
• CV documents uploaded by candidates must be in a text-readable format.
• Backend server and database must be operational and accessible at all times.
10. SYSTEM WORKFLOW
 Candidate Workflow
• Step 1: Candidate registers on the application with personal details.
• Step 2: Login credentials (username & password) are sent to the registered
email.
• Step 3: Candidate logs in using the received credentials.
• Step 4: Candidate uploads their CV through the application.
• Step 5: System automatically extracts relevant skills from the CV.
• Step 6: Job vacancies are displayed based on the extracted skills.
• Step 7: Candidate selects a suitable job and submits an application.
• Step 8: If approved by HR, candidate attends the MCQ evaluation test.
• Step 9: Final hiring decision is communicated after test evaluation.
 HR Workflow
• Step 1: HR logs in to the dedicated HR dashboard.
• Step 2: HR reviews the list of applicants and their uploaded CVs.
• Step 3: HR approves or rejects candidates based on CV review.
• Step 4: Approved candidates are directed to take the MCQ test.
• Step 5: HR evaluates MCQ results and makes final hiring decisions